// PARKED — see ../README.md, "What is parked, and why".
//
// Zoo edge: C11 <> LKMM (incomparable). Runnable now that LKMM is an operand,
// but kater cannot establish incomparability even in principle: incomparability
// needs a refutation in each direction, and a kater refutation proves nothing —
// the inclusion checks are sound but incomplete, so the counterexample path
// need not be realisable.
//
// Both directions are in fact refuted, which is consistent with the recorded
// verdict and is worth having on record, but it is corroboration, not evidence.
// The edge stays provenance: literature, with the two witnesses in
// litmus/incomparable/C11-vs-LKMM/ carrying it.
//
//   assert lkmm::hb <= c11-old::psc+
//     => [lkmm::Marked&DEP] addr [lkmm::Marked]
//   assert c11-old::psc <= lkmm::hb+     (the assert below)
//     => [SC&R] po [SC&R]
include "../../kat/c11-old.kat"
include "../../derived/lkmm.kat"

assert c11-old::psc <= lkmm::hb+
